    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves leans heavily into favorable matchups against mid-tier rotations, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01) leading the charge as our strongest plays. Both benefit from facing starters with xERAs above 4.30, providing a high floor for our core. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a massive 15% SP skill adjustment against a soft matchup, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees his projection bolstered by a significant 14% platoon edge. Further down the order, **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.46) are high-leverage starts; both are capitalized by the matchup against Ober, where their high SP skill adjustment and top-of-the-order positioning (1 and 2, respectively) maximize their potential for run production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s board was the final utility spot, where **Coby Mayo** (56.06) edged out **Jackson Merrill** (55.37) for the primary slot, though both remain in the starting nine. While **Jackson Merrill** is technically the \"bench\" of the outfield group due to a sub-optimal matchup against Cole, his 13% platoon edge against a right-handed starter keeps him relevant despite the tough SP skill environment. We are monitoring **Kyle Tucker** (66.85) and **Nasim Nunez** (53.34) closely, as both are subject to pending lineup confirmations. **Nasim Nunez** remains a vital component of our strategy; despite his #9 spot, the 85% SB-favorable delivery from the opposing pitcher makes him an essential \"scarcity\" play to secure stolen bases, even if his run-scoring ceiling is lower than the rest of the infield. \n\nRisks are concentrated at the bottom of the order and the top of the rotation. **Wade Meckler** (40.30) is the most precarious start of the day; facing Skenes, he is strictly a volume play whose value is heavily suppressed by the SP skill handicap. We are also wary of the **Henry Bolte** (43.75) start, as the negative park factor and tough matchup against Woo nearly pushed him to the bench. Our depth remains hampered by the IL presence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, forcing us to lean on prospects like **Coby Mayo** and **Sam Antonacci** to provide the necessary spark to hold our position in the Roto standings. We remain ready to pivot to bench depth like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Liam Hicks**, or **Luis Lara** should late-afternoon weather or lineup scratches shift the daily efficiency floor.",
